// The module map over chip A's COMMITTED header, by relative path into the
// crate rather than a copy.
//
// This is the whole point of the brief's "link it through a module map over
// the header": a signature that drifts is a COMPILE error here, at the call
// site, rather than a `@_silgen_name` declaration that agrees with nothing and
// crashes at run time. The iOS bridging header carries the same reasoning.
//
// The path is relative to THIS file: Sources/CParfastFFI -> apps/parfast/mac
// -> apps/parfast -> crates/parfast-ffi/include.
module CParfastFFI {
    header "../../../crates/parfast-ffi/include/parfast_ffi.h"
    export *
}
